From a353ee54948f65485ce8cee7c1c5080f4069db68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Delgado <328510259+thinkddr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:57:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(widget): a multi-line Entry spaces its rows by the
 theme's line spacing

RichText only added SizeNameLineSpacing between paragraphs, never between the rows
of one inline segment, which is all the text of an Entry: its rows stepped by the
font height alone, whatever the theme said. A multi-line Entry now asks for the gap
between every row (RichText.spaceRows), and the layout, the min size, the cursor,
the selection boxes and hit testing all step rows by font height + line spacing, as
a CSS line-height does. A single-line Entry and every other RichText are unchanged.

The Entry goldens with several rows move down by the test theme's spacing (4 px a
row); selection_enter grows past the viewport and shows its scroll bar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
